{
  "answer": "Durable per-query state is a status machine {not_started, partial, completed, failed} plus harvest_index, emitted_claim_ids, backend_calls, and integrity_sha256. Partial means 0 < harvest_index < harvest_total and is not completed. Resume skips only completed (no extra backend_calls). Partial continues from harvest_index. Failed retries the same harvest. A byte-flipped or inconsistent-completed checkpoint is refused (exit 2, REFUSE:checkpoint-*). That is not RES-0004 (fetch-body snapshots) and not RES-0171 (cache-key + staleness). A naive skip-of-anything-already-touched drops claims. SUCCESS:RES-0191",
